@startuml
title D-05 Assisted Payment Terminal Operating Modes

skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial

component "Assisted Payment Terminal\none app family / codebase" as APT
component "Mode 1:\nCashier-Assisted Terminal" as Cashier
component "Mode 2:\nContinuity Terminal" as ContinuityMode
component "Central PMS\npayment finality + exit authority" as Central
component "Site POS Server\nfiscal issuance authority" as POS
component "Operator Console\nsupervisor and audit controls" as Console
component "ExitPass Continuity\nBCP controls" as Continuity

APT --> Cashier : normal cashier-assisted operation
APT --> ContinuityMode : disabled by default

Cashier --> Central : payment context / assisted workflow
Cashier --> POS : fiscal issuance through resolved Site POS Server
Cashier --> Console : cashier accountability and audit

ContinuityMode --> Continuity : BCP activation required
ContinuityMode --> Console : supervisor approval / incident reference
ContinuityMode --> Central : controlled degraded operation
ContinuityMode --> POS : fiscal issuance when allowed

note right of ContinuityMode
Requires supervisor approval,
incident or BCP reference,
audit tagging, and reconciliation.
end note

note bottom of APT
Cashier POS and EC Device are not separate product families.
They are operating modes of one Assisted Payment Terminal family.
end note

@enduml
